# Feature: Pull Birds (Hazards)

Bird hazards fly across the sky. Shooting a bird incurrs a penalty and startles it away.

## Revision 1 (Legacy)
- No birds. Replays and scoring are clay-only.

## Revision 2
- 3–4 birds per game.
- Birds are spread through the full minute.
- Penalty: -10 points.
- Clay-first priority: shots resolve against clays first, then birds if no clay was hit. This ensures fairness if a bird overlaps a clay.

## Revision 3 (Current)
- 10–12 birds per game (roughly one every 5–6s).
- Maximum 2 birds on screen at once.
- Approximately 1/3 of games (34.4%) feature at least one moment with two birds overlapping on screen.
- Timing: Launches start between 60–201 ticks. Gaps are calculated to ensure the last bird exits before the round ends (run margin 240 ticks).
- Height Variety: Mostly clay heights (middle/lower bands), with a 1/5 chance of higher (40–80px) or lower (330–380px) trajectories.
- Bug Fixes:
  - Fixed timing where the last bird could launch too late to exit.
  - Fixed overlap chaining that could put 3+ birds on screen.
